AI Appointment Scheduling System

An AI-powered appointment scheduling workflow built with n8n, OpenAI, Telegram, Google Calendar, and Google Sheets.

The system analyzes customer messages, identifies appointment-related intent, checks calendar availability, and routes the request to the appropriate scheduling action.

This project was built as Deliverable 7 of my AI Automation portfolio.

⸻

Overview

The workflow allows customers to interact with an appointment scheduling system using natural language instead of forms or predefined commands.

Example:

Customer:

Hi, I’d like to book a dental cleaning on September 10 at 2 PM.

The system extracts the appointment information, checks the requested time against Google Calendar, and proceeds only when the slot is available.

⸻

Tech Stack

* n8n — Workflow automation and orchestration
* OpenAI — Intent classification and appointment information extraction
* Telegram — Customer messaging interface
* Google Calendar — Appointment availability and event management
* Google Sheets — Appointment records and event ID storage

⸻

Workflow Architecture

Telegram / Webhook
        ↓
Edit Fields
        ↓
OpenAI Appointment Analyzer
        ↓
Switch
        │
        ├── Book
        │     ↓
        │   Validate Date & Time
        │     ↓
        │   Check Calendar Availability
        │     ↓
        │   Available?
        │    ├── Yes → Create Event → Confirmation
        │    └── No  → Unavailable Notification
        │
        ├── Check Availability
        │     ↓
        │   Validate Date & Time
        │     ↓
        │   Check Google Calendar
        │     ↓
        │   Return Availability
        │
        ├── Reschedule
        │     ↓
        │   Find Existing Appointment
        │     ↓
        │   Check New Slot
        │     ↓
        │   Update Appointment
        │
        ├── Cancel
        │     ↓
        │   Find Existing Appointment
        │     ↓
        │   Cancel Calendar Event
        │
        ├── Appointment Question
        │     ↓
        │   Send Appropriate Response
        │
        └── Other
              ↓
            Fallback / General Inquiry Response

⸻

Supported Intents

The AI analyzes each incoming message and classifies it into one of six routes:

Book

Handles customers who want to create a new appointment.

Example:

I’d like to book a dental cleaning on September 10 at 2 PM.

Before creating the appointment, the workflow checks Google Calendar to prevent conflicting bookings.

Check Availability

Handles customers asking whether a particular appointment slot is available.

Example:

Is September 10 at 3 PM available for teeth whitening?

This route only checks availability and does not automatically create an appointment.

Reschedule

Handles requests to move an existing appointment to a new date or time.

Example:

Can you move my appointment to September 12 at 4 PM?

The new time is checked for availability before the existing appointment is modified.

Cancel

Handles customers who want to cancel an existing appointment.

Example:

Please cancel my dental cleaning appointment.

The workflow identifies the existing appointment and uses its Google Calendar Event ID to cancel the correct event.

Appointment Question

Handles questions specifically related to an appointment or the appointment process.

Example:

How long does a dental cleaning appointment usually take?

Other

Handles messages that do not require appointment scheduling actions.

Example:

How much does teeth whitening cost?

General service, pricing, payment, and unrelated questions are kept separate from appointment-management requests.

⸻

AI Structured Output

OpenAI converts natural-language messages into structured data that n8n can use for routing and scheduling.

Example:

{
  "intent": "book",
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "Unknown",
  "phone": "Unknown",
  "service": "dental cleaning",
  "requested_date": "2026-09-10",
  "requested_time": "14:00",
  "appointment_id": "Unknown",
  "reason": "Customer wants to schedule a dental cleaning.",
  "missing_information": [],
  "requires_calendar_action": true
}

Structured output makes the AI response predictable and allows downstream n8n nodes to reference individual fields reliably.

⸻

Appointment Availability

Appointments are configured with a one-hour duration.

For example, a customer requesting:

September 10 at 2:00 PM

results in an availability check for:

Start: 2026-09-10 14:00
End:   2026-09-10 15:00

The workflow checks this exact period against Google Calendar before creating the event.

If the slot is occupied, the workflow does not create another event.

⸻

Input Validation

The workflow does not rely solely on AI classification.

Before Calendar operations are performed, required scheduling information is validated.

For example:

requested_date != "Unknown"
AND
requested_time != "Unknown"

If required information is missing, the workflow asks the customer for the missing details instead of sending invalid data to Google Calendar.

This prevents incomplete appointment requests from causing Calendar API errors.

⸻

Appointment Tracking

Google Calendar acts as the source of truth for the actual schedule.

Google Sheets can be used as an appointment lookup and tracking layer.

Example fields:

telegram_user_id
name
username
service
requested_date
requested_time
event_id
appointment_status
last_action

When Google Calendar creates an appointment, the returned Event ID is stored with the customer’s appointment record.

This allows the workflow to identify the correct Calendar event when processing cancellations or rescheduling requests.

⸻

Example Test Cases

Branch	Example Input	Expected Result
Book	Book a dental cleaning on September 10 at 2 PM.	Check availability and create event if available
Book Conflict	Book a dental cleaning on September 10 at 2 PM.	Reject if the slot is already occupied
Availability	Is September 11 at 3 PM available?	Return availability without booking
Reschedule	Move my appointment to September 12 at 4 PM.	Check new slot and update appointment
Cancel	Please cancel my appointment.	Find and cancel existing event
Appointment Question	How long does a cleaning appointment take?	Route to appointment question
Other	How much does teeth whitening cost?	Route to general inquiry

